PARITY — what was shipped (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Data sources (P1/S8 seam, no view networking):
    getExtendedHealth (/system/health) + useConnectionPool (/dev-tools/runtime-info) + getVersionInfo
    (/system/version) → coalesced by BackendStatusSource.onUpdate(BackendStatusUpdate{health,pool,
    version,status,connection}); the three web interval-refetches become the source's refresh path,
    surfaced as the error-retry + the one-shot stale auto-refresh (the web accordion has no manual
    refresh — faithfully NOT invented). useTranslation → BackendStatusStrings facade (P1/S10).
  Shared components mapped to native counterparts:
    AccordionSection→BackendStatusAccordion (collapsible, defaultOpen, Server IconBox + title +
    description + trailing badge + rotating chevron, full a11y button), GlassPanel→.tsGlassPanel(),
    IconBox→TSIconBox, Badge(okCount/total healthy)→BackendHealthBadge (success when all ok else
    warning), DataTable→native Grid(regular)/cards(compact) with the 5 web columns (Status icon+text
    via getStatusIcon tone, Component, Latency `fmtNumber(_,1) ms`, Failures `fmtInt` danger-tinted
    when >0, Last Check `formatDateTime`|—), StatCard×5→BackendPoolTile grid (Max Open/Open/In Use/
    Idle/Wait Count), KVList→BackendRuntimeKVRow grid (Go Version/Uptime/Goroutines/OS-Arch with the
    web version→system fallback), Skeleton→TSSkeleton, FadeIn→TSFadeIn.
  States — every one renders (never a blank box):
    loading (two-block skeleton, web `<Skeleton h-48 + h-32>`) · content (the three sections; the
    component table owns the inline "No components found" web emptyMessage; pool + runtime sections
    gated exactly like web `{pool &&}` / `{(system||version) &&}`) · empty (resolved with NOTHING —
    no components, pool, or runtime → friendly ContentUnavailableView) · error (QueryError-equivalent
    + Retry) · stale (chip + ONE guarded auto-refresh, re-armed on live) · offline (cached snapshot +
    offline chip/banner, no refetch).
  i18n: every web key present in BackendStatusSection.strings — the 21 source labels (Backend Status,
    Component health…info, healthy, Component Health, Status, Component, Latency, Failures, Last Check,
    No components found, Database Connection Pool, Max Open, Open, In Use, Idle, Wait Count, System
    Runtime, Go Version, Uptime, Goroutines, OS / Arch) where the English label IS the key, plus the
    native envelope (Stale/Offline + banners, Expanded/Collapsed/Toggle Section a11y, Loading, empty,
    Couldn't load…, Retry). Every native string resolves via the facade — zero hardcoded English in code.
  a11y: VoiceOver labels on the accordion header button (combined title+description, Expanded/Collapsed
    value, hint, .isButton), the section summary (tally / empty / title-only), every component row +
    card (combined: status, name, latency, failures, last check), the health badge, the freshness chip,
    section titles as headers; Dynamic Type (system fonts) + reduce-motion (TSFadeIn/TSSkeleton + the
    accordion reveal/chevron) respected; macOS-safe size-class guard (#if os(iOS)).
  Telemetry: view.opened emitted once with surface slug "BackendStatusSection" (P1/S11), tested.

